{{also|MUFFIN|Muffin}}
==English==
[[File:Mmm...English_muffins_(5393409247).jpg|right|thumb|A muffin (sense 1, an [[English muffin]]).]]
[[File:Muffin_NIH.jpg|right|thumb|A muffin (sense 2) with a spreading [[muffin top]].]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmʌfɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-muffin.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌfɪn|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From earlier {{m|en|moofin}}, probably a diminutive of {{bor|en|nds|Muffe}} {{gl|"small cake"; {{m|nds|Muffen|pos=plural}}}}, from {{der|en|gml|muffe|t=small pastry}}. An alternative, and phonologically less plausible theory suggests a connection to {{ncog|fro|moflet|(pain) moflet|t=roll|lit=soft (bread)}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|British}} A type of [[flattish]] bun, usually cut in two [[horizontally]], [[toast]]ed and spread with butter, etc, before being eaten; an [[English muffin]].
#: {{syn|en|English muffin|q1=US}}
# {{senseid|en|cupcake}} A [[cupcake]]-shaped baked good (for example of [[cornbread]], [[banana bread]], or a chocolate dough), sometimes glazed but typically without frosting, eaten especially for breakfast (in contrast to a cupcake, which is a [[dessert]]).
#* {{seeCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[mechanism]] used in the [[w:Java Network Launching Protocol|Java Network Launching Protocol]] [[analogous]] to the [[cookie]] mechanism and which permits a program running in a [[browser]] to perform operations on a client machine.
#* '''2001''', ''JNLP and Java Web Start'', Sun Developer Network, Technical Articles and Tips, 30 May 2001:
#*: The name/value pairs provided by the PersistenceService are similar to browser cookies. The Java Web Start implementation honors this legacy by naming the pairs "'''muffins'''."
# {{lb|en|slang}} {{non-gloss definition|Term of endearment.}}<!--, e.g. "nuffin' muffin"-->
#: {{ux|en|I love you, '''muffin'''!}}
# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} The [[vulva]] or [[vagina]]; [[pubic hair]] around it.
#: {{syn|en|muffin|Thesaurus:vagina}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1986|artist=w:Mojo Nixon; w:Skid Roper|title=Stuffin' Martha's Muffin|album={{w|Frenzy (Mojo Nixon album)|Frenzy}}|passage=I wanna be stuffin' {{w|Martha Quinn|Martha's}} '''muffin'''!}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} A less [[talented]] player; one who [[muff]]s, or drops the ball.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A charming, attractive young man. <!--Ch1908: "one who dangles after a young woman"--> {{rfex|en}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[small]] [[plate]], smaller than a [[twiffler]]. <!--Chambers 1908-->
# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialect|Northern England|especially|Manchester}} A [[roll]], [[bap]] or [[cob]], which may or may not be flat or toasted.
# {{lb|en|ice hockey|slang}} A very weak [[shot]] in ice hockey where the [[puck]] does not travel fast.
# {{lb|en|Canada|slang|archaic}} A young [[woman#Noun|woman]] who would regularly accompany a particular man during a [[social season#Noun|social season]]. {{defdate|late 1800s}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Margaret Oliphant|Margaret Oliphant W&#91;ilson&#93; Oliphant]]||quotee=[[w:Laurence Oliphant (author)|Laurence Oliphant]]|title=Memoir of the Life of Laurence Oliphant and of Alice Oliphant, His Wife|edition=new|location=Edinburgh; London|publisher=w:William Blackwood and Sons|year=1854<!--in OED-->|year_published=1892|page=92|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/memoiroflifeofla00olipuoft/page/92/mode/1up|passage=I had a charming '''muffin''' yesterday. She is engaged to be married, so don't be alarmed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:William Howard Russell|W&#91;illiam&#93; Howard Russell]]|title=Canada: Its Defenses, Condition, and Resources|location=London|publisher=Bradbury and Evans|year=1865|page=149|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/canadaitsdefense00russ/page/149/mode/1up|passage=The fair Canadians may have been too kind in accepting the name and position of "'''muffins'''" from the young Britishry; but the latter cannot say they have suffered much in consequence. A '''muffin''' is simply a lady who sits beside the male occupant of the sleigh—''Sola cum solo'', "and all the rest is leather and prunella."|brackets=on}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Arthur Griffiths (author)|Arthur Griffiths]]|title=Fifty Years of Public Service|location=London{{nb...}}|publisher=[[w:Cassell (publisher)|Cassel and Company, Limited]]|year=1904|page=52–53|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/fiftyyearspubli00grifgoog/page/n72/mode/1up|passage=A long string of two-seated sleighs, a pleasant ''tête-à-tête'' drive for many miles snugly ensconced in the buffalo robes with your "'''muffin'''" by your side, a halt at some hospitable settler's, and an impromptu dance in his barn, wTith a return journey in the crisp moonlight air, left impressions that are still vivid. ¶ The "'''muffin'''" was a social institution of those days, which may or may not have survived. Every young swain by unwritten but acknowledged law was permitted to make his choice of a partner for the season, with whom he danced exclusively, and whom he drove in his sleigh and skated with hand in hand.}}

