{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To eat muffins.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Benjamin Disraeli|title=Benjamin Disraeli Letters: 1835-1837|location=Toronto; Buffalo; London|publisher=w:University of Toronto Press|year=1837|year_published=1982|page=319|isbn=0-8020-5587-7|passage=I dined yesterday at {{!}} three on mutton chops and 1/2 pint of E[ast] I [ndian] sherry, and then ''tead'' and '''muffined''' at 8.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Gingerbread Muffins Start Day Off Right|journal=The Calgary Herald|location=Calgary, Alta.|date=12 October 1965|page=39|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/481330254/|passage=And now comes a recipe guaranteed to keep the family happily '''muffined'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Concetta Doucette|title=Savings|journal=Impact|series=Albuquerque Journal Magazine|volume=10|issue=15|date=27 January 1987|page=13|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/157858046/|passage=NANCY SCRAPES OFF the mold without complaining because it is like a gift from Carl, and she doesn’t have the heart to tell him she is '''muffined''' out …}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Bea Lewis|title=For Teatime Or Anytime|journal=The Newsday Magazine|date=28 February 1988|page=35|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/722959876/|passage=HAVE YOU '''muffined''' out, had more than your share of croissants?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=Marlin E. Misner|title=History of the Reagan Home: The Boyhood Home in Dixon, Illinois|year=2005|page=35|isbn=9780977142200|passage=We met about 8:00 A.M. for the usual continental breakfast – I am getting over '''muffined'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jane Sigaloff|title=The Romancipation of Maggie Hunter|publisher=Red Dress Ink|year=2007|page=159|isbn=978-0-373-89549-6|passage=‘So what I can get you to celebrate. Bit of cake?’ ‘I’m all '''muffined''' up, thanks!’}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Carrie Ewin; Chris Ewin; Cheryl Ewin|chapter=Lesson 5: Creating Text Posts|title=Facebook for Seniors: Connect with Friends and Family in 12 Easy Lessons|location=San Francisco, Caif.|publisher=w:No Starch Press|year=2017|section=section “Viewing Your Posts on Your Timeline”|page=97|isbn=1-59327-791-1|passage=Hehe, I've eaten three apple muffins this morning. I've all '''muffined''' out!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To feed muffins to.
#* {{RQ:Worboise St Beetha's|chapter=The St. Beetha's Temperance Society|page=213|passage=But one or two evil-disposed characters muttered they might be sure the lady had her own turn to serve, and they might be sure they wasn't "teaed and '''muffined''' and sandwiched for nothing!"}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Working Woman|year=1999|page=96|passage=We were caffeined and '''muffined''' and then asked to seat ourselves at any of several large round tables.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Nancy Huston|title=Dolce Agonia|location=Toronto, Ont.|publisher=[[w:McArthur & Company Publishing|McArthur & Company]]|year=2001|page=102|isbn=1-55278-244-1|passage=Well, you know, my mother always told me to welcome new neighbors with muffins, and I just realized you’ve already been here six months and I still haven’t gotten around to baking muffins for you … Well anyway, that’s all I wanted to tell you — consider yourself '''muffined'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Earl Laman|chapter=20|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=7GfQEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT217|title=Being With…|location=Meadville, Pa.|publisher=Fulton Books|year=2023|isbn=979-8-88731-567-6|passage=Grandma Bessie saw me and '''muffined''' me.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become like a muffin; to increase in size.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Sophie Littlefield|title=w:A Bad Day for Sorry|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Minotaur Books|month=August|year=2009|page=48|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/baddayforsorry00litt/page/48/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-312-55920-5|passage=A pale band of flesh '''muffined''' up over her shorts, her lively top not quite up to the task of covering it, and Chrissy tugged at the fabric ineffectively.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author={{w|James Axler}} [house name; {{w|Nick Pollotta}}]|chapter=Prologue|title=Time Castaways|series=w:Deathlands|publisher=Worldwide Library|month=December|year=2009|page=16|passage=In spite of wearing the largest size of body armor available, her ample breasts were simply much too big, and deliciously '''muffined''' over the top.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=E[lizabeth] F[rancine] Winters|chapter=15|title=Sharks and Minnows|series=book one of The Jolie Chronicles|publisher=Kenspeckle Productions, LLC|year=2013|page=173|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sharksminnowsboo0000wint/page/173/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-940531-00-7|passage=Baby fat '''muffined''' over the top of Rebecca’s jeans.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Terry Dowling|chapter=The Four Darks|editor=w:Ellen Datlow|title=Fearful Symmetries: An Anthology of Horror|publisher=ChiZine Publications|year=2014|page=117|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/fearfulsymmetrie0000unse/page/117/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-77148-193-9|passage=Allan Grace was lean, but his neck '''muffined''' out over the crisp white collar.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:List of people who have walked across Australia#David Mason|David Mason]]|title=Walk Across Australia: The First Solo Crossing|publisher=Rosenberg Publishing|year=2014|isbn=9781925078244|passage=Beers rested on bellies that '''muffined''' over shorts.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Adam Biles|title=Feeding Time|publisher=Galley Beggar Press|year=2016|isbn=978-1-910296-74-5|passage=It may have been Nurse Agnes’ looping signature that touched him off, or the way flesh '''muffined''' from the pumps of the fat lady that boarded the bus at his stop every morning: a spark is a spark, and one was as good as any other.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make like a muffin.
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=[[w:The Windsor Magazine|The Windsor Magazine: An Illustrated Monthly for Men and Women]]|year=1920|page=418|passage=Twanty-two harrin’ and t’ree ship’s biscuits, '''muffined''' like! Ah, yew doan’t know what '''muffined''' biscuits be!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Edmund Vance Cooke|chapter=Fat|title=Companionable Poems|year=1924|page=183|passage=WE HAVE too many raisins in our cake; / Our bread is '''muffined'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=[[w:Harper's Bazaar|Harper’s Bazaar]]|year=1944|page=63|passage=Toques high as Queen Mary’s or low as a pillbox, extended and thickened and '''muffined''' at the edge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Caleb Pirtle|title=The Land Where We Belong|publisher=Leisure Time Publishing|year=1990|page=91|isbn=0-9626682-4-9|passage='''Muffined''' Eggs with Mushrooms}}

